config NRFMODULE_USB_VBUS_APP_OWNED_ENABLE
	bool "Application owns USB enable on debounced VBUS rise"
	depends on USB_DEVICE_STACK_NEXT
	default n
	help
	  Application takes over USB enable on debounced VBUS rise: the board
	  publishes the edge but does not enable USBD, so nothing is exposed to
	  the host until the application calls
	  nrfmodule_usb_vbus_enable_request(). The same holds for a boot with
	  VBUS already present. Use this when work must complete before the host
	  can see the device, for example refreshing the mass-storage FAT image.
	  The board still disables USBD by itself on a debounced VBUS fall.
